cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AMLET, please cite the article below and, if relevant, this
  software.
title: "AMLET: Another Mixed Logit Estimation Tool"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bastin
    given-names: Fabian
    email: fabian.bastin@gmail.com
version: 0.13.1-4
date-released: 2026-10-18
# all the versions archived on Zenodo; v0.13.1-4 is 10.5281/zenodo.23454087
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23454086
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fbastin/amlet-legacy"
abstract: >-
  AMLET estimates multinomial and mixed logit models by maximum simulated
  likelihood. It includes the adaptive Monte Carlo trust-region algorithms
  (BTR / BTRDA) developed by F. Bastin, C. Cirillo and Ph. L. Toint. This
  repository makes the last release, 0.13.1, build and run on current Linux
  systems, and fixes the bugs found on the way, including in the random
  number generator.
keywords:
  - mixed logit
  - discrete choice
  - maximum simulated likelihood
  - trust region
  - Monte Carlo
